      "text": "To solve the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\) and express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Take the natural logarithm (or any logarithm) of both sides of the equation:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7^{x+7}) = \\ln(8^x)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the logarithm power rule \\(\\ln(a^b) = b \\ln(a)\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   (x+7) \\ln 7 = x \\ln 8\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distribute and rearrange the equation to isolate \\(x\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   x \\ln 7 + 7 \\ln 7 = x \\ln 8\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   x \\ln 7 - x \\ln 8 = -7 \\ln 7\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   x (\\ln 7 - \\ln 8) = -7 \\ln 7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\(x\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{-7 \\ln 7}{\\ln 7 - \\ln 8}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the expression:**\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\ln 7}{\\ln 8 - \\ln 7}\n   \\]\n\n   Using the property of logarithms \\(\\ln a - \\ln b = \\ln \\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)\\), we get:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\ln 7}{\\ln \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Express \\(x\\) in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\):**\n\n   Recall that \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\) implies:\n\n   \\[\n   b^x = 7^7\n   \\]\n\n   From the previous step, we have:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\ln 7}{\\ln \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, we need to match \\(b\\) such that:\n\n   \\[\n   b^{\\frac{7 \\ln 7}{\\ln \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}} = 7^7\n   \\]\n\n   This implies:\n\n   \\[\n   b^{\\ln 7} = 7\n   \\]\n\n   Simplifying further:\n\n   \\[\n   b = e^{\\ln 7} = 7\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
