      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We start by taking the logarithm of both sides of the equation $7^{x+7} = 8^x$. This gives us:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\log(7^{x+7}) &= \\log(8^x) \\\\\n(x+7)\\log(7) &= x\\log(8)\n\\end{align*}\nExpanding the left side, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\nx\\log(7) + 7\\log(7) &= x\\log(8) \\\\\nx\\log(7) &= x\\log(8) - 7\\log(7)\n\\end{align*}\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nx\\log(7) - x\\log(8) &= -7\\log(7) \\\\\nx(\\log(7) - \\log(8)) &= -7\\log(7) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{-7\\log(7)}{\\log(7) - \\log(8)}\n\\end{align*}\nWe know that $\\log_a(b) = \\frac{\\log_c(b)}{\\log_c(a)}$, so we can rewrite the expression as:\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\frac{7\\log(7)}{\\log(8) - \\log(7)} \\\\\n\\log_8(7) &= \\frac{7}{b-1}\n\\end{align*}\nSince $\\log_a(b) = \\frac{\\log_c(b)}{\\log_c(a)}$, we can rewrite $\\log_8(7)$ as:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\log_8(7) &= \\frac{\\log(7)}{\\log(8)}\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\log(7)}{\\log(8)} &= \\frac{7}{b-1} \\\\\n\\log(7)\\log(8) &= 7(b-1) \\\\\n\\log(7)\\log(8) &= 7b - 7 \\\\\n7b &= \\log(7)\\log(8) + 7 \\\\\nb &= \\frac{\\log(7)\\log(8) + 7}{7}\n\\end{align*}\nRecognizing that $\\log_7(8) = \\frac{\\log(8)}{\\log(7)}$, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\nb &= \\frac{\\log(7)\\log(8) + 7}{7} \\\\\nb &= \\frac{\\log(7)\\cdot\\frac{\\log(8)}{\\log(7)} + 7}{7} \\\\\nb &= \\frac{\\log(8) + 7}{7} \\\\\nb &= \\boxed{1 + \\log_7(8)}\n\\end{align*}The final answer is: 1+\\log_7(8)",
